\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The measured robust--taper lattice for the main subarray, colored by $\eta $ (clamped at 5). The untapered column and the natural-weighting row appear as labeled sentinel bands on the otherwise log-scaled taper axis. Black contours mark skirt $=0.10$ (solid) and $0.25$ (dashed); their blockiness is lattice quantization, not a smoothing artifact. Red circles mark the lattice cells that anchor the default $s_0=0.10$ imaging curve. This lattice is essentially complete: of its 259 sampled points, 255 have status \texttt  {ok} and 4 are beam-capped.}}{13}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:heatmap}{{3}{13}{The measured robust--taper lattice for the main subarray, colored by $\eta $ (clamped at 5). The untapered column and the natural-weighting row appear as labeled sentinel bands on the otherwise log-scaled taper axis. Black contours mark skirt $=0.10$ (solid) and $0.25$ (dashed); their blockiness is lattice quantization, not a smoothing artifact. Red circles mark the lattice cells that anchor the default $s_0=0.10$ imaging curve. This lattice is essentially complete: of its 259 sampled points, 255 have status \texttt {ok} and 4 are beam-capped}{figure.3}{}}
